  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given, $\\quad y^{2}=2 d(x+\\sqrt{d})$\r\n$\\Rightarrow$\r\n2y $y_{1}=2 d \\Rightarrow d=y y_{1}$\r\nFrom Eq. (i),\r\n$$\r\ny^{2}=2 y y_{1}\\left(x+\\sqrt{y y_{1}}\\right)\r\n$$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad y^{2}-2 y y_{1} x=\\sqrt{y y_{1}} \\cdot 2 y y_{1}$\r\n$\\Rightarrow\\left(y^{2}-2 y y_{1} x\\right)^{2}=4\\left(y y_{1}\\right)^{3}$\r\nSo, degree of above equation is 3.",
    "image": null
  },
